# Line-ending policy (audit finding #9, 2026-07-28).
#
# .bat/.cmd MUST be CRLF in the working tree. cmd.exe's parser is line-ending
# sensitive: an LF-only batch file works for simple sequential commands (which
# is why scripts/daily_swing_paper.bat has run fine for 12 scheduled runs) but
# can mis-resolve labels/goto and multi-line blocks. This repo runs a .bat from
# Task Scheduler, so pin it rather than leave it to core.autocrlf.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Shell scripts must stay LF even on Windows -- CRLF breaks the shebang.
*.sh  text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf

# SQLite DBs and caches are binary; never let git touch their bytes.
*.db binary
